-- title:
--   Translation lift commuting with a level-spherical smoothing operator
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field, let $0<\alpha<\beta$ and let $\Phi_0$ be a slab fundamental domain: $\Phi_0$ lies in the determinant-norm slab between $\alpha$ and $\beta$ and is a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ acting on that slab with the restricted adelic Haar measure. Let $\sigma\in\mathbb R$ and let $\xi$ be a character of the full group of ideles with $\|\xi(z)\|=\|z\|^{\sigma}$ for all $z$. Let $U$ be a compact subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_F)$ arising as $U=O\cap\ker(\mathrm{glArch})$ for an open subgroup $O$, let `tys` be a family of archimedean types, and let $f$ be a test function which is factorizable (a product of an archimedean test factor and a finite test factor) and level-spherical of type `tys` at $U$, i.e. $f(g)=f_\infty(g_\infty)\cdot\mathbf 1_{U_{\mathrm{fin}}}(g_{\mathrm{fin}})$ with $f_\infty$ an archimedean test factor, bi-finite of the given type, and invariant under conjugation by the archimedean row-isometry inclusions at every infinite place. Let $T_c$ be a bounded operator on the cuspidal sub-carrier (the closed subspace generated by the classes of continuous cuspidal members of weight $\xi$) which, on every class $[\varphi]$ of a cuspidal member, returns the class of $\varphi * f$ whenever $\varphi * f$ is again a cuspidal member. Then for every infinite place $w$ and every $k$ in the project's row-isometry subgroup `rowIsometrySubgroup₀` of $F_w$ there is a bounded operator $S$ on the cuspidal sub-carrier with $S\circ T_c=T_c\circ S$ and such that for every cuspidal member $\varphi$ the right translate of $\varphi$ by the inclusion of $k$ at $w$ is again a cuspidal member and $S[\varphi]$ is its class. The compactness of $U$ and the openness of $O$ are assumed, but $f$ enters only through factorizability and level-sphericality.
--
--   This provides the commuting pair consisting of a right-translation operator by an archimedean row isometry and a smoothing operator given by convolution with a level-spherical test function, both realised on the cuspidal sub-carrier. It is used in the Schur-type dichotomy for irreducible cuspidal subrepresentations, [`AutomorphicForm.CuspidalSpectrum.map_inf_orthogonal_eq_bot_or_le_of_isIrreducibleCuspSubrep`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.CuspidalSpectrum.map_inf_orthogonal_eq_bot_or_le_of_isIrreducibleCuspSubrep).
